it, and for financed deals, a breakdown of Finance Bank usage — both as a table and as a chart."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a salesperson leaderboard panel showing volume, total margin and average margin per deal side by side, so 'best' is never reduced to one number the viewer can't question."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Add a discount panel: total and average discount given, trended by month, split by Scheme Applied."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "Add a panel showing what share of billed/closed deals used each Scheme Applied value, ranked."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "Add a monthly trend panel showing volume and total margin together, so a viewer can see months where they move in opposite directions (like Oct/Mar in this dataset)."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "Add a branch comparison panel: volume, margin, conversion and below-floor rate, all four metrics per branch in one view."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "Add an average sale price panel, sliceable by Model, Branch and Variant Tier."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4 — Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format — Word, PDF, Notion, a README, doesn't matter) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow** — how you actually went from the raw export to your cleaned data to your SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made (especially how you resolved salesperson identity); (2) **Key Discoveries** — your top 3–5 findings, stated as a decision-maker would want to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations** — at least 3 concrete, data-backed recommendations for what Sanchay Motors should actually do next. This document is the deliverable a hiring manager or client would actually read — treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S1", "text": "Build a single composite salesperson scorecard combining volume, margin, conversion and below-floor discipline into one number. Defend your weights."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Model the enquiry-to-booking gap: do faster-closing deals earn better or worse margins?"}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Find the model/colour/variant combinations with the longest delivery waits, and check whether the Lost-deal remarks mention waiting as a reason."}]}], "premium": [{"id": "X5", "text": "**Quantify discount effectiveness.** Does a higher discount actually buy a proportionally higher conversion rate, or is the group over-discounting relative to what it earns back in closed deals? Quantify the relationship, not just describe it."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Forecast next quarter.** Using the 12 months of history, forecast Q1 FY26-27 (Apr-Jun 2026) volume and margin per branch with a simple time-series or regression approach. Identify which branch is trending best once you control for the December spike."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Normalize it.** Design a 3NF relational schema (separate tables for salespeople, branches, and deals at minimum) from the flat file, load it into a real SQL database, and rewrite your S3 and S9 answers as proper JOIN queries instead of operating on one flat table."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Prove the branch gap is real.** Janakpuri and Dwarka show roughly 2.5× the below-floor rate of the best branches. Run a statistical test (e.g. a chi-square or two-proportion z-test) to determine whether this gap is significant or explainable by each branch's own floor-setting policy — and show your work."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Build and defend a scorecard.** Construct a weighted composite salesperson score from volume, margin, conversion and discipline. Run a sensitivity analysis showing how the ranking changes as you vary each weight by ±10%, and state which weighting you'd actually recommend to management and why."}]}$pack$::jsonb
