ding."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a — Dashboard Page 1: Deal Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D5", "text": "Make the deal-lookup results table itself filterable/sortable by any visible column, so someone can browse instead of only searching by exact Deal ID."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same lookup screen, show customer context: family size, customer type, accessories taken, the face-to-face feedback reason, and any remarks."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for Branch, Salesperson, Model, Status and Payment Mode that combine with the date filters (AND logic) rather than replacing them."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a search box that takes a Deal ID and returns everything about that one deal on a single screen: salesperson + branch, car (model/variant/tier/fuel/colour/model year), the full price chain (ex-showroom → floor → quoted → discount → final), payment/finance detail, and the delivery timeline (enquiry → booking → scheduled → actual, with the gap called out)."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a date-range filter on Booking Date and a separate date-range filter on (Scheduled or Actual) Delivery Date, and make sure both can be applied together."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b — Dashboard Page 2: Analytics", "tasks": [{"id": "D12", "text": "Add a finance panel: Payment Mode split, and for financed deals, a breakdown of Finance Bank usage — both as a table and as a chart."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "Add a branch comparison panel: volume, margin, conversion and below-floor rate, all four metrics per branch in one view."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a salesperson leaderboard panel showing volume, total margin and average margin per deal side by side, so 'best' is never reduced to one number the viewer can't question."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "Add a panel showing what share of billed/closed deals used each Scheme Applied value, ranked."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "Add an average sale price panel, sliceable by Model, Branch and Variant Tier."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "Add a panel on Safety Rating: what share of Closed deals were on 5-star vs 4-star rated models, and what share of *feedback reasons* actually cite the safety rating — these are two different numbers, show both."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "Add a monthly trend panel showing volume and total margin together, so a viewer can see months where they move in opposite directions (like Oct/Mar in this dataset)."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect a global date-range filter (Booking Date), so the whole analytics page can be viewed for any period, not just the full year."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Add a discount panel: total and average discount given, trended by month, split by Scheme Applied."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Add an accessories panel: share of customers who showed interest vs who actually bought accessories vs who came back post-delivery, and the total revenue (and implied profit, at a margin % you define and state) each stage represents."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4 — Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format — Word, PDF, Notion, a README, doesn't matter) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow** — how you actually went from the raw export to your cleaned data to your SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made (especially how you resolved salesperson identity); (2) **Key Discoveries** — your top 3–5 findings, stated as a decision-maker would want to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations** — at least 3 concrete, data-backed recommendations for what Sanchay Motors should actually do next. This document is the deliverable a hiring manager or client would actually read — treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S1", "text": "Build a single composite salesperson scorecard combining volume, margin, conversion and below-floor discipline into one number. Defend your weights."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Model the enquiry-to-booking gap: do faster-closing deals earn better or worse margins?"}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Build a simple funnel: enquiry → booking → closed → delivered, with drop-off at each stage, split by branch."}]}], "premium": [{"id": "X2", "text": "**Prove the branch gap is real.** Janakpuri and Dwarka show roughly 2.5× the below-floor rate of the best branches. Run a statistical test (e.g. a chi-square or two-proportion z-test) to determine whether this gap is significant or explainable by each branch's own floor-setting policy — and show your work."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Build and defend a scorecard.** Construct a weighted composite salesperson score from volume, margin, conversion and discipline. Run a sensitivity analysis showing how the ranking changes as you vary each weight by ±10%, and state which weighting you'd actually recommend to management and why."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Forecast next quarter.** Using the 12 months of history, forecast Q1 FY26-27 (Apr-Jun 2026) volume and margin per branch with a simple time-series or regression approach. Identify which branch is trending best once you control for the December spike."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Quantify discount effectiveness.** Does a higher discount actually buy a proportionally higher conversion rate, or is the group over-discounting relative to what it earns back in closed deals? Quantify the relationship, not just describe it."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Normalize it.** Design a 3NF relational schema (separate tables for salespeople, branches, and deals at minimum) from the flat file, load it into a real SQL database, and rewrite your S3 and S9 answers as proper JOIN queries instead of operating on one flat table."}]}$pack$::jsonb
from public.datasets where slug = 'tata-delhi-sales-fy2526'
on conflict (license_code) do nothing;

