son."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Estimate what the December clearance actually cost the group in margin versus what it earned in volume and cleared inventory."}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Build a simple funnel: enquiry → booking → closed → delivered, with drop-off at each stage, split by branch."}]}], "premium": [{"id": "X2", "text": "**Prove the branch gap is real.** Janakpuri and Dwarka show roughly 2.5× the below-floor rate of the best branches. Run a statistical test (e.g. a chi-square or two-proportion z-test) to determine whether this gap is significant or explainable by each branch's own floor-setting policy — and show your work."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Forecast next quarter.** Using the 12 months of history, forecast Q1 FY26-27 (Apr-Jun 2026) volume and margin per branch with a simple time-series or regression approach. Identify which branch is trending best once you control for the December spike."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Build and defend a scorecard.** Construct a weighted composite salesperson score from volume, margin, conversion and discipline. Run a sensitivity analysis showing how the ranking changes as you vary each weight by ±10%, and state which weighting you'd actually recommend to management and why."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Normalize it.** Design a 3NF relational schema (separate tables for salespeople, branches, and deals at minimum) from the flat file, load it into a real SQL database, and rewrite your S3 and S9 answers as proper JOIN queries instead of operating on one flat table."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Quantify discount effectiveness.** Does a higher discount actually buy a proportionally higher conversion rate, or is the group over-discounting relative to what it earns back in closed deals? Quantify the relationship, not just describe it."}]}$pack$::jsonb
