on panel: volume, margin, conversion and below-floor rate, all four metrics per branch in one view."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Add an accessories panel: share of customers who showed interest vs who actually bought accessories vs who came back post-delivery, and the total revenue (and implied profit, at a margin % you define and state) each stage represents."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "Add a panel on Safety Rating: what share of Closed deals were on 5-star vs 4-star rated models, and what share of *feedback reasons* actually cite the safety rating — these are two different numbers, show both."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect a global date-range filter (Booking Date), so the whole analytics page can be viewed for any period, not just the full year."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a salesperson leaderboard panel showing volume, total margin and average margin per deal side by side, so 'best' is never reduced to one number the viewer can't question."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4 — Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format — Word, PDF, Notion, a README, doesn't matter) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow** — how you actually went from the raw export to your cleaned data to your SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made (especially how you resolved salesperson identity); (2) **Key Discoveries** — your top 3–5 findings, stated as a decision-maker would want to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations** — at least 3 concrete, data-backed recommendations for what Sanchay Motors should actually do next. This document is the deliverable a hiring manager or client would actually read — treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S6", "text": "Check whether higher family_size correlates with higher accessories spend — do bigger households buy more add-ons?"}, {"id": "X-S2", "text":